<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'

import StageHint from './lib/StageHint.abide'
import stageHint from './lib/StageHint.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import StarHint from './lib/StarHint.abide'
import starHint from './lib/StarHint.abide' with { type: 'text' }
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={['/components/menu', '/helpers/popover']}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/pipeline/lib/StageHints.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a stage is described by its hint, with nothing written beside it'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/pipeline/lib/StageHints.test.ts',
            from: ["test('focus opens the hint at once and Escape closes it'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/pipeline/lib/StageHints.test.ts',
            from: ["test('a pointer resting on a stage opens its hint'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/e2e/chart.spec.ts',
            from: [
                'test("a pointer moving under a chart\'s readout keeps it open — 50.47"',
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Explain a pipeline stage on hover and on focus">
        <p>Spread <code>tooltip.tip</code> on the element it explains, and the text describes it from
            the first paint. Nothing is written beside it, so it
            works in a list, a table row or a flex row alike. Give the element a
            <code>tabindex</code> where it is not focusable, or a keyboard never reaches the
            hint. The hint shows in the popover the root layout spreads <code>tooltip.host</code>
            on.</p>
        <Example code={stageHint}><StageHint /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Open a hint under its anchor, with no wait">
        <p><code>side</code> is where the hint goes, flipped where there is no room.
            <code>delay</code> is how long a pointer rests before it opens. A click does not
            open it at once; a key that moves focus to the element does.</p>
        <Example code={starHint}><StarHint /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Show every hint of the app in one popover">
        <p>Call <code>tooltip.host</code> from your root layout's script, spread its
            <code>hint</code> part onto an element there, and write its <code>text</code> inside.
            Every <code>tooltip.tip</code> on every page opens in it, one at a time, in the top
            layer, so no scroller clips it. The element and its classes are yours.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import { tooltip } from '@abide/abide'

            const hints = tooltip.host()
            </script>

            <html lang="en">
                <body>
                    <slot />
                    <span {...hints.hint} class="m-0 w-max max-w-60 rounded-md px-3 py-2">
                        {hints.text}
                    </span>
                </body>
            </html>
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Draw an arrow pointing at the anchor">
        <p>The popover carries the side it took as <code>data-side</code>, and
            <code>--arrow-offset</code> is where along that edge the anchor's middle falls.
            <code>arrowInset</code> on a <code>tooltip.tip</code> keeps the arrow off the rounded
            corners.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <span
                {...hints.hint}
                class="m-0 overflow-visible rounded-md px-3 py-2
                before:absolute before:left-(--arrow-offset) before:size-2
                before:-translate-x-1/2 before:rotate-45 before:bg-raised
                data-[side=top]:before:-bottom-1
                data-[side=bottom]:before:-top-1"
            >{hints.text}</span>
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
